.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-INIT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-init ,
.Nm bootchartd ,
.Nm halt ,
.Nm "busybox init" ,
.Nm linuxrc ,
.Nm poweroff ,
.Nm reboot
.Nd BusyBox startup and shutdown tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm bootchartd
.Cm start
.Op Ar PROG ARGS
.Nm bootchartd
.Cm stop
.Nm bootchartd
.Cm init
.Nm halt
.Op Fl d Ar DELAY
.Op Fl nfw
.Nm init
.Nm linuxrc
.Nm poweroff
.Op Fl d Ar DELAY
.Op Fl nf
.Nm reboot
.Op Fl d Ar DELAY
.Op Fl nf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the init applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Pa /sbin/init
is the project's
.Xr init 8 ,
not the BusyBox applet.
On os-real,
.Nm halt ,
.Nm poweroff ,
and
.Nm reboot
stop the machine through
.Xr reboot 2 ;
the standalone shell dispatches these applets before searching the file system.
.Bl -tag -width bootchartd
.It Nm bootchartd
Collect boot chart data in
.Pa /var/log/bootchart.tgz .
This applet has no use on Rach2.
.It Nm halt
Halt the system.
.It Nm init
Run as the first process at boot, starting and restarting children according
to
.Pa /etc/inittab
without exiting.
Rach2 uses its own init instead.
.It Nm linuxrc
Run BusyBox init from an old-style Linux initrd without requiring process ID 1.
This applet has no use on Rach2.
.It Nm poweroff
Halt the system and turn off power.
.It Nm reboot
Restart the system.
.El
.Ss bootchartd commands
.Bl -tag -width start
.It Cm start Op Ar PROG ARGS
Start logging in the background.
If
.Ar PROG
is given, run it, then stop logging with
.Dv SIGUSR1 .
.It Cm stop
Send
.Dv SIGUSR1
to all bootchartd processes.
.It Cm init
Start logging in the background and stop when getty or xdm is seen.
This form is for init scripts.
.El
.Pp
As process ID 1,
.Nm bootchartd
logs as for
.Cm init ,
then executes the program specified by
.Ev bootchart_init ,
.Pa /init ,
or
.Pa /sbin/init .
.Ss BusyBox init
The following describes the unused BusyBox applet.
It is intended to be started by the kernel.
It does not support multiple runlevels.
.Pp
Signals control it as follows:
.Bl -tag -width SIGTSTP
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload
.Pa /etc/inittab .
.It Dv SIGTSTP
Stop restarting children until
.Dv SIGCONT .
.It Dv SIGQUIT
Execute another init.
.It Dv SIGUSR1
Halt.
.It Dv SIGTERM
Reboot.
.It Dv SIGUSR2
Power off.
.It Dv SIGINT
Run the Ctrl-Alt-Del action.
.El
.Pp
An
.Pa /etc/inittab
entry has the form:
.Dl id:runlevels:action:process
.Bl -tag -width runlevels
.It Ar id
Controlling terminal, appended to
.Pa /dev/ .
An empty field uses init's standard input and output.
The field need not be unique, though repeated terminal names may cause
unexpected results.
.It Ar runlevels
Ignored.
.It Ar action
One of
.Cm sysinit , respawn , askfirst , wait , once , restart , ctrlaltdel ,
or
.Cm shutdown .
.It Ar process
Program and command line to execute.
.El
.Pp
The
.Cm sysinit
actions run first and must finish before the
.Cm wait
actions run.
Each
.Cm wait
action must finish before init continues.
The
.Cm once
actions run without waiting, followed by the
.Cm respawn
actions.
A
.Cm respawn
action restarts whenever its process exits, without a restart rate limit.
The
.Cm askfirst
action does the same, but prints
.Ql Please press Enter to activate this console.
and waits for Enter before starting the program.
.Pp
The
.Cm restart
action executes a replacement init, normally
.Pa /sbin/init ;
it may instead run a script.
The
.Cm ctrlaltdel
actions run on Ctrl-Alt-Del, and the
.Cm shutdown
actions run when init is told to reboot.
Within each action type, entries run in file order.
Unknown actions produce an error message and are skipped.
.Pp
Without
.Pa /etc/inittab ,
BusyBox init uses these entries:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::askfirst:/bin/sh
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/sbin/swapoff -a
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::restart:/sbin/init
tty2::askfirst:/bin/sh
tty3::askfirst:/bin/sh
tty4::askfirst:/bin/sh
.Ed
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options apply to
.Nm halt ,
.Nm poweroff ,
and
.Nm reboot :
.Bl -tag -width "-d SEC"
.It Fl d Ar SEC
Delay the action by
.Ar SEC
seconds.
.It Fl n
Do not call sync before the action.
.It Fl f
Call
.Xr reboot 2
directly instead of going through init.
.El
.Pp
The
.Nm halt
usage also lists:
.Bl -tag -width "-d SEC"
.It Fl w
Write a wtmp record only.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/log/bootchart.tgz
.It Pa /sbin/init
The project's init program on Rach2.
.It Pa /etc/inittab
Configuration for BusyBox init.
.It Pa /var/log/bootchart.tgz
Boot chart data written by
.Nm bootchartd .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reboot 2 ,
.Xr init 8
